    <string name="combination_caveat">Synergies are design suggestions. Rare pairs reflect incomplete annotations, not proof of a unique idea.</string>
    <string name="synergy_expedition">Expedition loadout: limited space and supplies make every crafted item a trade-off.</string>
    <string name="synergy_survival">Survival loop: crafting turns scarce supplies into a choice between immediate needs and future safety.</string>
    <string name="synergy_loadout">Loadout puzzle: choosing what to craft also means choosing what to carry.</string>
    <string name="synergy_heist">Improvised heist: destruction opens new routes but can expose the player.</string>
    <string name="synergy_physics">Physical puzzle: object properties become the tools for solving a problem.</string>
    <string name="synergy_deck">A new plan each run: rebuild the deck around the opportunities of the current attempt.</string>
    <string name="synergy_team">Against the clock: shared deadlines encourage role division and coordination.</string>
    <string name="synergy_farm">Daily rhythm: planting, tending and harvesting form a readable planning cycle.</string>
    <string name="synergy_discovery">Discovery through conversation: clues from people guide exploration, and discoveries unlock new questions.</string>
    <string name="synergy_rhythm">Movement as music: jumps become a sequence the player can learn and perform to a beat.</string>
    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy and data</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">GameReel stores generated ideas, notes, presets, imported libraries and preferences on your device. No account is required. The app contains no advertising or analytics SDK and does not send this content to a GameReel server.\n\nThe app goes online only for the game pack catalog and pack pictures: it downloads pack files from GitHub and pictures from the game publishers’ servers. These requests carry no personal data; the servers see ordinary request details such as your IP address. If you tap “Suggest for catalog” in the pack editor, the pack and your optional comment are sent through Google Apps Script to the developer and published as a public pull request on GitHub. Nothing is sent without that tap. System backups may include app data, depending on your device settings. Delete ideas and presets in the app; Android app settings let you clear all app data. Browser data can be removed in the browser settings.\n\nImport reads only the file you select. Opening external links is handled by your browser, under the destination website’s policy. The web version’s hosting provider may process ordinary HTTP request logs.\n\nGame names and source links identify reference examples. GameReel is not affiliated with the referenced studios or stores. Combination suggestions are design hypotheses; rarity in the collection does not prove that an idea is unique.</string>
